gguf-rco step 6h, fifth part (0042): one kernel, one op, one launch per layer.
Every tile-type layer goes through the grouped kernel: at load the tile-type
shards of a layer (a run of consecutive ones; the whole tensor of a
single-type layer is a run of one) are packed into one buffer with the
descriptor tables of the splits the launch can choose, the shards' tiles
become views into it; apply calls one op for the run - the activations
quantised once per 256 (the sixth form on every type), every tile writing
its own output columns, the split-K partials summed in one fp32 kernel.
A Q2_K or IQ1_M shard stays on the row path beside its group. Applies
after 0038 (0040's op is superseded; its patch is not applied).

